            0.142
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Which mode of travel is used by the most number of students?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.149,
            0.86,
            0.171
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• Which mode of travel is used by the least number of students?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.176,
            0.885,
            0.221
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A pictograph represents data through pictures of objects. It helps answer questions about data with just a quick glance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.223,
            0.885,
            0.292
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In the above pictograph, one unit or symbol ( ) is used to represent one student. There are also other pictographs where one unit or symbol stands for many people or objects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.309,
            0.886,
            0.378
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Example:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Nand Kishor collected responses from the children of his middle school in Berasia regarding how often they slept at least 9 hours during the night. He prepared a pictograph from the data:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.173,
            0.386,
            0.876,
            0.536
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "table_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.173,
                0.386,
                0.876,
                0.536
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_6_table_6.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tbody><tr><td>Response</td><td>Number of Children ( = 10 Children)</td></tr><tr><td>Always</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Sometimes</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Never</td><td></td></tr></tbody></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.166,
            0.55,
            0.769,
            0.573
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Answer the following questions using the pictograph:",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.576,
            0.884,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. What is the number of children who always slept at least 9 hours at night?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.628,
            0.883,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. How many children sometimes slept at least 9 hours at night?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.657,
            0.884,
            0.704
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "3. How many children always slept less than 9 hours each night? Explain how you got your answer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.716,
            0.271,
            0.737
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Solutions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.748,
            0.885,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. In the table, there are 5 pictures for ‘Always’. Each picture represents 10 children. Therefore, 5 pictures indicate 5 × 10 = 50 children."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.822,
            0.887,
            0.892
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "2. There are 2 complete pictures (2 × 10 = 20) and a half picture (half of 10 = 5). Therefore, the number of children who sleep at least 9 hours only sometimes is 20 + 5 = 25."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "page_number",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.086,
            0.942,
            0.113,
            0.959
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "80"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
